What is this and what does it do?
----------------------------------

Today  in  History simply displays some birthdays and events which happened
on  the current day sometime in history.  best of all its FREE!  However if
you  feel  like sending me 1/2/3 or more UKP for it then feel free, I don't
mind ;-)

What machine specs do I need?
-----------------------------

It should run on any Amiga from OS1.3 through to OS3.1, please inform me if
this  is  not  the  case.  I'm running OS3.0 with an 030/50 CPU and it runs
fine.

**** I'm running OS3.1 with an 040/33 now

What BBS software will it run on?
---------------------------------

Any BBS software that can run DOS doors. It uses no specific commands for
any particular BBS software. There are a few ANSI characters dotted about
the program. These help in positioning and colourisation of the final
display. There are NO backdoors in this program.

How do I install it?
--------------------

Installation couldn't be simpler :-) You've already done the hard part by
unpacking the archive.  Now all you need to do is move the entire History
directory to your Doors:  directory.  History requires it's data files are
found in Doors:History/data/

What do I do now?
-----------------

History is now ready to use. Add History as a CLI door to your BBS. When
History is run it will display it's information at runtime. There too many
types of BBS programs out there for me to tell you how this should be
achieved, so I won't waste your time trying.

I've done that now what?
------------------------

Thats  it  :-)  You have fully installed Today In History.  If for whatever
reason it doesn't appear to be working please recheck all the above and try
again.  It DOES work :-)

